    "synthesis": "Jackknife sensitivity analysis demonstrates that Fold 2 OOF temperature (T=1.1603) is highly stable across its 22 calibration races, exhibiting a small standard deviation of 0.0343 and a low coefficient of variation of 2.96%. Fold 1 OOF temperature (T=0.9385) displays moderate stability (std = 0.0554, CV = 5.91%) due to its smaller sample of 11 races. Neither fold exhibits single-race catastrophic sensitivity. Because Fold 1 relies on N=11 races, temperature scaling should be treated as exploratory rather than authoritative. Uncalibrated softmax (T=1.0) represents a cleaner, parameter-free reference, under which candidate w=0.20 also retains decisive, statistically significant superiority over the grid baseline (Delta = -0.2507, p = 5.49e-05)."
